// Arrival scene at Cabillonum with Theron in the party: his brother lives
// here. If he thinks little of the player, or the player has joined the
// house, he sells them out to his family and goes home.
=== start
[opinion theron < 0] -> sells
[flag house_factor] -> sells
~ quest theron_debt start
Theron stops at the gate and looks down the long street to the river, at the warehouses and the boats and a stone house with a blue door near the quay.

"My brother lives there," he says. "Demarchos. He lends money to Vettius, the money Vettius lends to soldiers." He doesn't look at you. "And I owe the family for a ship of wine. I'd rather not talk about the ship." He straightens his cloak. "But if you want to hurt the house without lifting a sword, he's the one to talk to. I'll come with you. I'll even be polite."
* "Thank you, Theron." -> END

=== sells
~ quest theron_debt failed failed; set theron_sold; set house_warned
Theron stops at the gate and looks down the long street to the river, at the warehouses and the boats and a stone house with a blue door near the quay.

"My brother lives there," he says. "I'm going to see him. Alone." He turns to you, and he isn't smiling. "I'll tell you what I'm going to tell him, because I'm a Greek, not a thief. I'm going to tell him what you're here to do to the house of Vettius, because my brother lends Vettius money, and because I owe my family more than I owe you." He hitches his pack on his shoulder. "Then I'm going home to Massilia. Goodbye."
* "Theron." -> gone
* Let him go. -> gone

=== gone
~ part; leave
He goes down the street toward the blue door, and doesn't look back.
